Neither the bootloader nor the UKIs will remain unchanged with time. Updates to
either systemd-boot or the kernel will trigger either a new EFI binary being
copied to the EFI system partition or a rebuild of the associated UKI. Every
time this happens, the respective files need to be resigned. To make this
happen, we are using a mkinitcpio hook (for the UKI) and a pacman hook (for
systemd-boot).

To make sure that both the pacman and mkinitcpio hook are working, we will not
sign anything manually but create the hooks and run them to trigger the signing
process.